course: dictionary
lesson: 6826
title: Ottawa, the capital of Canada
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Ottawa is a proper noun. It is the name of a place, so it starts with a capital letter. Look at the clues in this sentence: «Ottawa is the capital of Canada, and Canada is the second-largest country in the world.» The words capital of Canada tell you that Ottawa is a city, and it is the most important city in the country.
explain: Many people think the capital of Canada is Toronto or Montreal. Those are big cities, but they are not the capital. Ottawa is the capital, in the province of Ontario, on the Ottawa River. When you meet a place name, check the clues around it, then check a map or dictionary to be sure.
explain: The Ottawa River is a different thing from the city, though it has the same name. It is a big river between Ontario and Quebec. The city and the river are both called Ottawa because the name comes from the Ottawa (Odawa) people, an Indigenous people of North America.
fact: Ottawa is the capital city of Canada.
fact: Ottawa is in the province of Ontario, on the Ottawa River.
fact: The Ottawa River is a big river between Ontario and Quebec.
fact: Canada's Parliament meets in Ottawa, on Parliament Hill.
fact: In winter, the Rideau Canal in Ottawa freezes and becomes a very long skating rink.
exercise: «Ottawa is the capital of Canada, and Canada is the second-largest country in the world.» What is Ottawa? | An Indigenous people of North America | A mountain in the north | *The capital city of Canada | A river in Quebec
exercise: Many people say the capital of Canada is Toronto. Which city is the capital? | Montreal | *Ottawa | Vancouver | Toronto
exercise: The Ottawa River runs between which two places? | Alberta and Manitoba | *Ontario and Quebec | Ontario and Nova Scotia | Quebec and Yukon
test: The name Ottawa comes from which people? | The people of Toronto | The French explorers | *The Ottawa (Odawa), an Indigenous people of North America | The Canadian Parliament
test: «Canada's Parliament in Ottawa looks a bit like London's.» Where does Canada's Parliament meet? | London | *Ottawa | Toronto | Montreal
exam: In which province is the city of Ottawa? | *Ontario | British Columbia | Alberta | Quebec
